# Intro
An isolated, thin gas disc with young massive stars, to exercise the
HEALPix-cone HII scheme (`GEARFeedback:HII_angular_nside: 1`, 12 cones per
star) in a geometry closer to a dwarf galaxy than the single-star boxes
of the sibling examples.

The gas follows an exponential radial profile (scale length 150 pc,
truncated at 5 scale lengths) and a Gaussian vertical profile (sigma 20 pc).
It holds 4e6 Msun in 2e5 particles of 20 Msun, starts at 100 K, at rest,
with Z = 0.02 Zsun. The central density is about 17 H/cm^3, above the
`HII_min_density_Hpcm3` floor of 1 H/cm^3. There is no self-gravity and no
rotation. Sixty-three single stars of 10 to 40 Msun (Salpeter slope) are born
at t = 0: one Gaussian cluster of 62 stars (sigma 4 pc) and one field star.
The cluster centre sits in the mid-plane (z = 0) at a random radius of 0.3 to
1.5 scale lengths. The field star is drawn from the gas profile within 2 scale
lengths.

`Stars:HII_max_search_radius` (`max_search_radius` in `run.sh`, in kpc) is the
largest radius the HII search may reach around a star. It caps the size of
an ionised region. With fixed cones the arms of the pattern described below
extend up to this cap, so the strength of the pattern grows with it. Set it
with e.g. `max_search_radius=0.15 ./run.sh`.

`HII_random_cone_frame_per_star: 0` keeps the 12 cones fixed to the box axes,
so all stars share the same cone directions. `HII_random_cone_frame_per_star: 1`
rotates each star's cone frame by a random rotation fixed by its ID. Compare
the two settings with `run_name` (see Run).

# What to expect
With fixed cones the ionised region of the cluster is a square aligned with
the box axes, with lobes along the diagonals (an "X"). With
`random_frame=1` the region is round. The face-on panel of the figure shows
the difference.

# Configure
```
./configure --disable-mpi --with-chemistry=GEAR_10 --with-feedback=GEAR --with-cooling=grackle_1 --with-stars=GEAR --with-sink=GEAR --with-star-formation=GEAR --with-tracers=GEAR --with-kernel=wendland-C2 --with-grackle=path/to/grackle --with-chealpix=path/to/chealpix
make -j
```
`--with-chealpix` is required for `HII_angular_nside` of 1 or more. The default
`--with-number-of-hii-angular-pixels=12` fits `HII_angular_nside: 1`.

# Run
```
./run.sh                    # cones fixed to the box axes
random_frame=1 ./run.sh     # random cone frame per star
```
`run.sh` builds the initial conditions with `makeIC_disc.py`, fetches the
Grackle and radiation tables, runs SWIFT to 1 Myr (4 threads by default) and
calls `plot_hii_disc.py` on the final snapshot. Use `run_name=<name>` to keep
the outputs of a run, e.g. one per cone-frame setting. Disc mass, scale
length, scale height, cluster layout and star counts are environment
variables listed at the top of `run.sh`; `python3 makeIC_disc.py --help`
lists the generator options.

# Plot
`plot_hii_disc.py -s snap/snapshot -i <index>` writes a figure with the disc
face-on (top) and edge-on (bottom). Grey is the gas surface density, the
colour scale is the surface density of HII-tagged gas, and the stars are
marked.
